  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"1.5.1\"\n\npackage:\n  name: pacparser\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/manugarg/pacparser/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 88dda1833b5c467ea61d0217fa58fbc7980f7c5a856ca2af325e6a110b1c081d\n  patches:\n    # The statically linked QuickJS needs pthreads, which glibc < 2.34\n    # does not provide as part of libc\n    # https://github.com/manugarg/pacparser/pull/250\n    - patches/250.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip:\n    - win\n  dynamic_linking:\n    overlinking_behavior: error\n    overdepending_behavior: error\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - make\n  run_exports:\n    - ${{ pin_subpackage('pacparser', upper_bound='x') }}\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      strict: true\n      bin:\n        - pactester\n      lib:\n        - pacparser\n      include:\n        - pacparser.h\n      files:\n        - share/man/man1/*\n        - share/man/man3/*\n        - share/doc/pacparser/**\n        # support files for the compilation test below\n        - etc/conda/test-files/**\n  - script:\n      - pactester -p $PREFIX/share/doc/pacparser/examples/wpad.dat -u http://www.example.com/\n      - $CC $CFLAGS $LDFLAGS tests/test_pacparser.c -lpacparser -o test_pacparser\n      - ./test_pacparser\n    requirements:\n      build:\n        - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    files:\n      recipe:\n        - tests/\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://pacparser.manugarg.com/\n  license: LGPL-3.0-or-later AND MIT\n  license_file:\n    - COPYING\n    - LICENSE.quickjs\n  summary: Library to parse proxy auto-config (PAC) files\n  description: |\n    pacparser is a library to parse proxy auto-config (PAC) files. Proxy\n    auto-config files are a vastly used proxy configuration method these\n    days. Web browsers can use a PAC file to determine which proxy server\n    to use or whether to go direct for a given URL. The package also ships\n    the pactester command line tool to test PAC files. The bundled\n    QuickJS-ng JavaScript engine (MIT) is statically linked into the\n    library with its symbols hidden.\n  repository: https://github.com/manugarg/pacparser\n  documentation: https://pacparser.manugarg.com/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - chrisburr\n",
